An OpenAI-compatible LLM provider whose external integration configures no secret now sends a placeholder API key rather than none. litellm builds an OpenAI client for that provider type, and that client raises "Missing credentials" locally - before any request leaves the process - when it has no key at all, so the unauthenticated on-premises endpoint ADR 0006 makes a first-class case could not make a single call. A real OpenAI or Anthropic provider with no key still sends none, and fails with the provider's own message on the record.
